From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:17:25 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 63/66] Plutonium: xdg_activation_v1, apps raise their windows
 through the shell

Apps raise each other's windows with xdg_activation_v1: a terminal opens
a link in a browser that is already running, a second launch of a
single-instance app brings up its window. Exo had no such global.

A token is valid if the client that committed it had keyboard focus
(the surface and serial it names aren't checked), and for 60 s; each is
used once. Activating a toplevel with a valid token notifies
EmbeddedWindows' observers (OnEmbeddedWindowActivationRequested), and
the broker asks the shell that owns the window's group, else the
visible shell, to show it: the "windowfocusrequest" event the overlay
uses. The shell isn't switched to.
